        "date": "2026-11-07T23:25:46Z"
      },
      "message": "feat: align a work offset 3-2-1 from a face, an edge and a vertex or bore\n\npick::align_321 reads the open operation's picks as datums: a flat face\nsets Z (its outward normal), a straight edge sets X (projected into the\nface's plane), a vertex or a bore's centre sets the origin (projected\nonto the face; else the edge's start). The frame goes to the WCS pane's\nslot through the existing undoable SetWcs command. The Geometry page\noffers \"Align WCS (3-2-1)\" under the picks, dark with the refusal as\nits tooltip until the picks qualify. Shell snapshots move by that\nbutton only.\n\nFixes #187\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
